<p>In the latest development in the Israel–Hezbollah conflict, Israeli ground forces crossed into southern Lebanon in multiple places and seized additional positions along the border. Israeli leaders and military commanders signaled that the plans include the option of pushing deeper into Lebanon. Israel has framed the move as a way to protect border communities from rocket and drone fire, and officials also described a broader goal: disarming Hezbollah. They said the incursion had been planned in advance. Hezbollah resumed launching rockets into Israel after a pause that Le Monde described as the first since 2024, and then struck for a second consecutive day as Israel carried out waves of airstrikes and widened its ground operation—pulling Lebanon deeper into the fighting. The escalation has intensified fears of a wider ground war and triggered fresh displacement in Lebanon, even as civilians on both sides say they want better security and an end to cross-border attacks.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/8pE161HIR8uZZTj2JThggQBIYQtYvnxDjOvAZ87FQ4zkd8OR70819B2nknEWVimXWENR6FydoAa8EpnpHl2OfDbxIydJKrK0oKhu16H0g5JYGIzrITPAcO28UcisU3Sm6dOjBCow5ZCJlgQOBZ92uWIN5bdXqdy88vnSQcnLlsf2M-9uYzSYOadbNLm5DgiLONH22lmGv0kzY28QqlpLdi8Mnzs301XeAvg' alt='Israeli soldiers near the border with Lebanon on Monday.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Multiple crossings: Israeli troops crossed from Israel into southern Lebanon at four locations, The Globe and Mail reported.</li><li>Stated tactical aim: The Globe and Mail said Israel is trying to push Hezbollah back from the border area—beyond its broader message about protecting northern communities.</li><li>Hezbollah’s calculus: Analysts quoted by The New York Times said Hezbollah’s renewed attacks look especially risky given its weakened position; one called it “practically a suicide mission”.</li><li>Iran linkage: Several reports cast Hezbollah’s actions as tied to Iran, placing the Lebanon front within a wider regional confrontation.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Israeli military and officials: Israeli officials have emphasized protecting northern Israeli communities, while Israel’s military chief described a more ambitious objective—disarming Hezbollah. Officials also said the incursion plans were prepared well in advance and include the option of going deeper into Lebanon. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/03/world/middleeast/israel-lebanon-deeper-incursion.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Hezbollah and supporters: Hezbollah fired rockets and missiles into Israel after a lull, presenting the strikes as support for Iran. Supporters also rallied in Beirut in solidarity with Iran. (<a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/02/world/middleeast/lebanon-hezbollah-israel-strikes.html'>The New York Times</a>)</li><li>Lebanese public sentiment (reported): BBC reporting described anger among many Lebanese who say Hezbollah’s actions have pulled the country into renewed war and mass displacement as Israel steps up its campaign. (<a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4gq3ykg7pvo'>BBC</a>)</li><li>Border community voices in Israel (reported): Le Monde reported that residents near the Lebanon border see the latest flare-up as part of the wider confrontation with Iran, and are watching closely to see whether Israel’s expanded operations change the security reality along the frontier. (<a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/03/at-the-border-with-lebanon-israelis-hope-for-the-end-of-hezbollah_6751065_4.html'>Le Monde</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/03/03/world/middleeast/israel-lebanon-deeper-incursion.html'>Israeli Plans Include Option of Going Deeper Into Lebanon, Officials Say</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/03/at-the-border-with-lebanon-israelis-hope-for-the-end-of-hezbollah_6751065_4.html'>At the border with Lebanon, Israelis hope for the end of Hezbollah</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-israel-expands-war-southern-lebanon-hezbollah/'>Israel expands war with incursion into southern Lebanon to push Hezbollah back</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.reuters.com/world/asia-pacific/australia-says-defence-personnel-safe-after-drone-attack-near-dubai-air-base-2026-03-03/'>Following a series of drone and rocket attacks by Hezbollah, the Israeli military launch a ground offensive into Lebanon, capturing several positions along the Israel—Lebanon border. (7 Israel)</a> - reuters.com</li><li><a href='https://www.bbc.com/news/articles/c4gq3ykg7pvo'>Battered and isolated, Hezbollah drags Lebanon into another war</a> - bbc.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/middle-east/lebanon-sucked-deeper-into-war-as-hezbollah-israel-trade-blows'>Lebanon sucked deeper into war as Hezbollah, Israel trade blows</a> - straitstimes.com</li></ul>